Date: Sat, 13 Nov 1993 16:58:48 -0500 (EST)
From: LEVY%BESSIE@venus.cis.yale.edu
Subject: META: Defaming the ExI Board

To Lefty, Sandy, and others who are concerned about the implications of the James 
Donald case:

What upset the ExI board about Mr. Donald's posting was the following comments:

> I know nothing of the financial probity of the Exi
> officers, other than that they have been accused of being
> barkers and stooges for a cryonic Ponzi scheme.  (I do not
> endorse or believe this accusation - it is mere hearsay -
> but I am unwilling to trust them with money.)

This is a textbook example of the kind of language that ruins people's reputations.  
The speaker (writer) repeats a wild accusation (that I and the other Board members 
are "barkers and stooges for a cryonic Ponzi scheme"), using the passive voice 
("have been accused") to free himself of the responsibility of citing his source.  
Then he disavows any endorsement or belief in the accusation, in an attempt to 
relieve himself of the responsibility for the damage that his words have already 
begun.  

The fact that this irresponsible behavior was targeted at the Directors of the 
organization that started and maintains this list is only part of the reason for our 
being upset with what Mr. Donald did.  I cannot speak for the other Board members, 
but I myself do not approve of language like this being used in reference to 
*anyone* on this list, and I would recommend that Harry take punitive measures in 
any such case where the matter was brought to my attention.  The fact that Mr. 
Donald -- incredibly, in my opinion -- managed to slight seven List members at once, 
and that they were the very people who devote time and money to maintaining the 
organization that makes the List possible, was more than enough justification for 
taking punitive action (preventing him from posting for 14 days).  According to 
Harry, Mr. Donald violated the terms of this agreement, posting within the 14 day 
limit.  Finally, he has apparently succeeded in forging Perry's address to send 
messages to the List (unless Perry is sending self-damaging messages and signing 
them as Donald, which I consider extremely unlikely).  Perhaps I should wait for the 
instigator of such acts to personally visit my office and defecate on my VAXStation 
before I recommend more serious action.

If you think that, after these incidents, it makes any sense to allws James Donald 
to remain this List, I can only conclude your sense of justice and fair play is so 
different from basic extropian values that your time is being wasted here.  

Simon! Levy
ExI Director



