Date: Sat, 13 Nov 93 12:24:45 PST
From: hfinney@shell.portal.com (Hal Finney)
Subject: I'm unsubscribing

I have been a subscriber to the extropians list for over two years now,
but in recent months I have found my interests turning elsewhere.  I don't
have time now to keep up with the list while doing the other things that
are important to me.  I do fully support the Extropian philosophy and plan
to continue to be a member of ExI.

I should mention that the timing of this decision is motivated in part by
recent list events.  The incessant flamewars we had until a few weeks
ago left a bad taste in my mouth.  The arbitrary system of list punishments
seems to have come to a head with the James Donald affair.

Ray and others are right: the list really is a totalitarian
dictatorship.  That's fine, for those who run it, and those who agree
with the king's policies.  I have had my disagreements over the years
with list policies, and my opinions have had no influence.  But I have
always understood that voluntary cooperation was a basic principle of
extropianism, and that the proper response in a situation like this is,
as has recently been suggested, to take your business elsewhere.

I don't know why it is that extropianism, a philosophy which in my mind
promotes tolerance and diversity, seems to attract the intolerant and
argumentative.  Even on the cypherpunks list the intolerant voices, who
speak up to quash debate or flame an ignorant poster, are usually
extropians.  I find a tremendous difference between the philosophy as
described in the pages of Extropy and as practiced here on the list.

I know that the character of the list changes over the months, as people
come and go.  I will try re-subscribing in a little while and see if the
taste of the list is more to my liking.  In the mean time, I wish list
members good luck; while we may disagree on tactics I know that we are
in close agreement on final goals.

Hal Finney
hal@alumni.caltech.edu
hfinney@shell.portal.com

