Here is something worthy of this group's careful consideration:
If all my connection with real events is through this medium,
via messages, opinions, rhetoric, divergent views, electronic
publications, etc., what may be known?  I think it was Churchman
who said that some kinds of inquiring systems need a guarantor --
some agent whose truthfulness depends on faith since measures
of proof would have to be in some larger system which would 
require a guarantor ...
Where may truth be found?  Shall we have truth-sayers, bound 
by some solemn oath to say things precisely as they see them and
never otherwise?  Shall we have some  particular reference
group list "The TRUTH List" on which all others may depend?
... or perhaps a standard language (Latin?) in which no one
ever lies   or states less than what they believe to be
the case?  And even then, does the summation of all the
strong beliefs add up to TRUTH?  Have we ever had it, or 
have we known things only statistically all along?
I'm hopeful -- the technology may provide us new validation
means and get us closer to the "real" state of things than
ever before -- however so many voices intervene...
Good luck with this one..
